00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:25.760
VO 2: It now resides in Lena and Kane, who will live on to change the world even further.

00:07:26.020 --> 00:07:30.629
VO 3: However, since Kane is a duplicate from the Shimmer, the Shimmer still remains in him.

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:34.800
VO 4: They're bound to have a kid eventually who will be even more Shimmer-like.

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:36.400
DAN: Oh, my god!

00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:41.800
If you were discussing the ending of the movie without discussing these scenes

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:45.480
and how they inform the meaning of the final shots,

00:07:45.580 --> 00:07:48.600
you aren't actually discussing the ending of the movie.

00:07:48.600 --> 00:07:50.640
You're writing fanfiction.

00:07:50.640 --> 00:07:52.340
This is how you get "Jarhead" sequels

00:07:52.350 --> 00:07:56.280
Do you want "Jarhead" sequels? Cause this is how you get "Jarhead" sequels.

00:07:56.300 --> 00:07:59.400
VO 8: He trains for 70 consecutive days.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:03.000
He gets to know every inch of his M16A4 rifle.

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:07.260
Then, he earns the right to be called a jarhead.

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:12.540
SPEAKER 1: Love being a Marine! Oorah!

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:17.380
DAN: At their elemental level, the themes and ideas

00:08:17.380 --> 00:08:20.600
that "Annihilation" grapples with aren't exactly new.

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:23.640
Now, I'm not a huge fan of "The Hero with a Thousand Faces."

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:26.480
I think it tries too hard to flatten culture

00:08:26.480 --> 00:08:31.160
and make an interesting observation about narrative patterns into a universal truth,

00:08:31.160 --> 00:08:36.120
but it is fair to say that "Annihilation" is a journey in a very classical sense,

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:38.160
and borrows from the broadest strokes.

00:08:38.180 --> 00:08:40.920
There is a call to adventure, a wizened sage,

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:44.900
a fellowship, and the crossing of a very literal threshold.

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:48.240
And indeed, change is central to Campbell's monomyth;

00:08:48.320 --> 00:08:52.740
the hero returns home triumphant but in some way no longer belongs

00:08:52.740 --> 00:08:56.240
because they have changed, home has changed, or both,

00:08:56.240 --> 00:08:59.180
and the new is incompatible with the old.

00:08:59.420 --> 00:09:02.400
Heroes return not as pig farmers, but as kings.

00:09:02.420 --> 00:09:05.860
Luke can't go back to the farm because the farm has been destroyed,

00:09:05.860 --> 00:09:07.760
and he's being swept up in a rebellion.

00:09:07.790 --> 00:09:11.820
The Vault Dweller can't return to the vault because their time in the Wasteland

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:14.680
has filled them with too many radical ideas.

00:09:14.940 --> 00:09:19.060
Frodo must go into the West because he no longer belongs in Middle-earth.

00:09:19.320 --> 00:09:22.300
You've got a lot of loss of innocence, a lot of war,

00:09:22.300 --> 00:09:24.440
and a lot of loss of innocence in war.

00:09:24.900 --> 00:09:30.480
So, yeah, the idea that the very act of going on a journey changes you isn't new.

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:34.360
"Annihilation," however, rejects the prelapsarian ideal.

00:09:34.360 --> 00:09:36.940
Lena doesn't start the movie innocent.

00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:42.379
There isn't a state of grace to fall from, and she doesn't return home as

00:09:42.660 --> 00:09:46.780
Campbell's Warrior, Lover, Emperor, Redeemer, or Saint.

00:09:46.780 --> 00:09:50.220
Indeed, "Annihilation" asks a far more challenging question:

00:09:50.220 --> 00:09:56.000
What if you return home and you're different, but you're still just you?

00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:59.280
At the end of her tribulations, Lena has been changed,

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:02.580
has been altered, but is still Lena.

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:04.960
Indeed, counter to Campbell's Hero,

00:10:04.960 --> 00:10:09.100
it is the very fact that home has changed in equal portion to herself

00:10:09.100 --> 00:10:12.220
that enables Lena to return in the first place.

00:10:17.940 --> 00:10:19.840
Before we go on, this is a good moment

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:21.820
to talk about the point of ambiguous endings

00:10:21.820 --> 00:10:23.760
and narrative ambiguity in general.

00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:27.560
The purpose of ambiguity is to frustrate the audience,

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:31.260
to deny a clean sense of diegetic closure

00:10:31.260 --> 00:10:35.260
and thusly force engagement with the metaphorical.

00:10:35.300 --> 00:10:39.820
Most ambiguous endings make perfect sense if you read them thematically,

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:43.480
and nine times out of ten, the diegetic answer is obvious

00:10:43.480 --> 00:10:45.900
once you approach the ending from this direction.

00:10:45.900 --> 00:10:49.020
If you approach the final shots of "Annihilation" thematically,

00:10:49.020 --> 00:10:51.840
the meaning of this moment is very obvious.

00:10:51.860 --> 00:10:54.340
But if you resist a thematic reading,

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:58.000
then you're going to get caught up in weird nonsense circles

00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:02.860
asking if the Shimmer is an alien terraforming device, as though the next movie,

00:11:02.940 --> 00:11:07.540
"Annihilation 2," is going to be a bunch of rainbow aliens coming down in spaceships,

00:11:07.540 --> 00:11:10.000
getting into gunfights with Aaron Eckhart.

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:14.440
Okay, let's be honest, Gerard Butler.

00:11:14.440 --> 00:11:18.920
On this journey, the fate of the five women reflects a variety of possible outcomes

00:11:18.920 --> 00:11:23.180
in the face of catastrophe and pain, each an extension of their trauma.

00:11:23.420 --> 00:11:26.920
Cassie is the victim of fate, killed through no fault of her own

00:11:26.920 --> 00:11:29.180
when a bear drags her off into the night

00:11:29.180 --> 00:11:33.060
and she is unwillingly consumed into the catastrophe.

00:11:33.060 --> 00:11:35.900
This is an echo of Cassie's own words from earlier.

00:11:35.960 --> 00:11:40.780
The person she used to be was destroyed by the loss of her daughter to leukemia,

00:11:41.100 --> 00:11:45.400
itself an event that she could neither prevent nor escape.

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:50.020
At the end of the day, we are all a roll of the dice away from disaster.

00:11:50.160 --> 00:11:53.020
Anya the addict is likewise consumed,

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:55.980
but where Cassie was the unfortunate victim of bad luck,

00:11:56.060 --> 00:12:01.440
Anya provokes her fate, allowing her rage and paranoia to overcome her

00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:04.880
before fully self-destructing at the hands of an outside force.

00:12:05.420 --> 00:12:07.880
Josie, in contrast, gives in peacefully,

00:12:07.880 --> 00:12:11.800
embracing her own oblivion and simply vanishing into the plant life,

00:12:11.800 --> 00:12:14.660
content with never knowing the things she doesn't know.

00:12:14.940 --> 00:12:19.300
She observes that Ventress wants to face the Shimmer and Lena wants to fight it,

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:21.540
but she wants neither of those things.

00:12:21.540 --> 00:12:25.020
She is willing to trade closure for harmony.

00:12:25.160 --> 00:12:28.660
In her final moments, she discards her long-sleeve shirt for a tank top,

00:12:28.660 --> 00:12:33.600
wearing her scars honestly, at peace with revealing her secret self to Lena

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:36.580
as she first absorbs greenery into herself

00:12:36.580 --> 00:12:40.040
before being absorbed seamlessly into the greenery.

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:42.980
Josie isn't just metaphorically in harmony with the Shimmer,

00:12:42.980 --> 00:12:45.260
which is to say her damage.

00:12:45.320 --> 00:12:48.100
She becomes one with the Shimmer.

00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:52.420
Ventress is dying of cancer, a woman at war with her own body

00:12:52.420 --> 00:12:56.840
and at war with the changes that confronting mortality impose on who she is.

00:12:56.840 --> 00:13:00.320
When Lena catches up to her at the lighthouse at the epicenter,

00:13:00.320 --> 00:13:04.160
the Shimmer, like the cancer, is already inside her

00:13:04.160 --> 00:13:06.240
and here in the holy of holies,

00:13:06.240 --> 00:13:10.960
at last Ventress and Lena confront the thing only to discover that pain

00:13:10.960 --> 00:13:16.240
is ultimately an unknowable, indescribable thing, a consuming force

00:13:16.240 --> 00:13:18.400
that refracts everything it touches

00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:21.660
and turns us into dark reflections of ourselves where,

00:13:21.660 --> 00:13:26.440
left unchecked, it becomes the singular thing, consuming everything

00:13:26.440 --> 00:13:30.240
until even the component parts are no longer recognizable.

00:13:30.780 --> 00:13:35.440
VENTRESS: Our bodies and our minds will be fragmented into their smallest parts, until

00:13:35.900 --> 00:13:37.900
not one part remains.

00:13:39.270 --> 00:13:44.210
DAN: Ventress is destroyed from within by her own cells betraying and consuming her.

00:13:45.210 --> 00:13:47.860
Finally, in Lena's confrontation with the being,

00:13:47.860 --> 00:13:49.120
she first tries to run

00:13:49.120 --> 00:13:51.760
but is unable to escape and is nearly suffocated.

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:59.140
It is not until she accepts that the being, that the pain and trauma is a part of her, a reflection of her,

00:13:59.140 --> 00:14:02.400
that she is able to confront it directly and destroy it,

00:14:02.400 --> 00:14:05.600
allowing her to escape and reunite with Kane.

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:08.600
The horror of "Annihilation" is existential

00:14:08.600 --> 00:14:10.940
and rooted firmly in the ordinary.

00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:13.820
It is film confronting the gradual ways that we are changed

00:14:13.820 --> 00:14:16.040
by the things and people around us,

00:14:16.040 --> 00:14:19.520
the ways that we slowly drift from one state into another,

00:14:19.520 --> 00:14:24.380
the terror of waking up one day to realize that we've become someone else -

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:26.420
someone we don't recognize.

00:14:26.420 --> 00:14:28.300
It is about life-changing events,

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:31.620
both the big and dramatic and the slower, subtler kind:

00:14:31.620 --> 00:14:33.780
the pain of losing a child

00:14:33.780 --> 00:14:38.300
and also the relationship that gradually slides into alienation.

00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:41.800
References to cancer are particularly important in the film.

00:14:41.800 --> 00:14:45.260
Lena teaches pre-med students about the biology of cancer.

00:14:45.260 --> 00:14:47.200
Cassie's daughter died of leukemia,

00:14:47.260 --> 00:14:51.480
and Ventress has some unspecified but terminal cancer.

00:14:51.480 --> 00:14:55.820
The opening monologue ruminates on the idea of cancer as immortal,

00:14:55.820 --> 00:14:58.820
cells that have had their self-destruct code turned off.

00:14:58.820 --> 00:15:03.520
Healthy, productive cells die, while toxic, deadly cells live forever,

00:15:03.520 --> 00:15:07.500
consuming, devouring, absorbing and corrupting.

00:15:07.500 --> 00:15:09.620
This extends into the metaphor as an irony.

00:15:09.660 --> 00:15:13.220
Why is it that everything we live for dies

00:15:13.220 --> 00:15:16.260
while our pain gets to be immortal?

00:15:16.500 --> 00:15:18.780
The Shimmer itself is a stand-in

00:15:18.780 --> 00:15:22.900
for trauma, depression, terminal disease, addiction, alienation, grief,

00:15:22.900 --> 00:15:27.200
and every other moment in our lives that leaves us unmoored from ourselves.

00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:29.580
This absorption is realized literally,

00:15:29.580 --> 00:15:33.940
with characters physically absorbing elements of each other as the film progresses.

00:15:33.940 --> 00:15:37.800
No better is this encapsulated than in the ouroboros tattoo,

00:15:37.860 --> 00:15:41.680
Anya has a tattoo of an ouroboros on her left forearm,

00:15:41.840 --> 00:15:44.400
a detail that's present from the beginning of the film

00:15:44.400 --> 00:15:46.380
but difficult to catch until later,

00:15:46.380 --> 00:15:48.619
as the film gradually calls attention to it.

00:15:48.619 --> 00:15:51.200
The key turning point comes when the expedition

00:15:51.200 --> 00:15:53.740
reaches the former headquarters of the Southern Reach.

00:15:53.740 --> 00:15:56.680
In one of the film's few overtly horrifying scenes,

00:15:56.680 --> 00:16:00.480
the women come across a data card left behind by the previous expedition.

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:04.760
On the card is a video file showing the team flaying one of their own,

00:16:04.760 --> 00:16:08.280
a solider with an ouroboros tattoo just like Anya's,

00:16:08.280 --> 00:16:11.680
revealing his intestines writhing like a coil of snakes.

00:16:11.839 --> 00:16:14.360
The final remains of this soldier are then found

00:16:14.360 --> 00:16:17.620
encased in lichen and mold growing into the wall of the pool.

00:16:17.620 --> 00:16:21.380
[♪♪]

00:16:21.380 --> 00:16:24.460
Anya and the soldier are of the same.

00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:28.400
That is the meaning, or at least a meaning, of the shared tattoo.

00:16:28.700 --> 00:16:31.100
In the soldier, she sees herself.

00:16:31.100 --> 00:16:34.680
She realizes this fear, references it explicitly

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:37.600
when she later ties up the surviving members of the team.

00:16:37.600 --> 00:16:42.280
ANYA: If I let you go and you tied me to a chair and cut me open,

00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:47.820
are my insides gonna move like my fingerprint?

00:16:49.840 --> 00:16:55.000
DAN: Her fear is that she has become like and as the soldier on the wall,

00:16:55.000 --> 00:16:57.480
but really she already was.

00:16:57.480 --> 00:16:59.980
Then, in Lena's darkest moment,

00:16:59.980 --> 00:17:03.360
her absolute nadir following the deaths of Cassie and Anya,

00:17:03.360 --> 00:17:06.680
Ventress' departure, and Josie's transformation,

00:17:06.680 --> 00:17:11.080
when she is the most alone, the tattoo appears on her arm.

00:17:11.900 --> 00:17:17.800
Lena has absorbed something of Anya, something that she will carry for the rest of her life.

00:17:17.960 --> 00:17:21.180
This is a good place perhaps to postulate on whether the solider

00:17:21.180 --> 00:17:26.160
already had the tattoo before entering the Shimmer, or if it is in some way a

00:17:26.440 --> 00:17:29.480
manifestation of the Shimmer, and the answer is

00:17:29.480 --> 00:17:30.800
that it doesn't matter.

00:17:30.800 --> 00:17:36.180
Because no matter what the diegetic answer may be, the symbol has taken on meaning

00:17:36.180 --> 00:17:39.400
through its association with each of the characters.

00:17:39.400 --> 00:17:43.580
Where it came from is irrelevant next to what it indicates.

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:46.320
The impact individuals have on one another,

00:17:46.320 --> 00:17:50.380
how we become impressed into each other and entwined,

00:17:50.380 --> 00:17:54.440
the ways that we see ourselves, our fates, in complete strangers,

00:17:54.440 --> 00:17:58.420
a cycle of exchange without beginning or end.

00:17:58.940 --> 00:18:01.920
Life changes us in unpredictable ways.

00:18:01.920 --> 00:18:04.700
We absorb our environments and the people around us

00:18:04.700 --> 00:18:07.600
and as horrifying as that sounds it's -

00:18:08.420 --> 00:18:10.280
SPEAKER 2 [offscreen]: Nightmarish?

00:18:10.280 --> 00:18:11.740
LENA: Not always.

00:18:13.480 --> 00:18:15.820
Sometimes it was beautiful.

00:18:16.260 --> 00:18:19.000
And this is the note that "Annihilation" chooses to go out on,

00:18:19.240 --> 00:18:24.500
recognizing that there is an existential horror to the nature of intimate relationships,

00:18:24.500 --> 00:18:27.620
that opening ourselves to others, allowing them in,

00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:31.260
brings with it an annihilation of our singular self.

00:18:31.340 --> 00:18:35.560
We merge, we reshape, we combine and replicate and mirror,

00:18:35.560 --> 00:18:37.760
and on a level that is terrifying.

00:18:37.820 --> 00:18:42.240
To be with someone is to sacrifice something of who you are.

00:18:42.520 --> 00:18:44.680
But it's also beautiful.

00:18:44.680 --> 00:18:46.020
In the final moments,

00:18:46.020 --> 00:18:50.020
Lena and Kane confront the fact that they are no longer the people they used to be.

00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:54.800
They have both changed dramatically, radically, since their relationship began.

00:18:54.800 --> 00:19:00.080
Their slow drift apart, Lena's infidelity, Kane's absence and his nearly fatal illness

00:19:00.140 --> 00:19:04.880
have compounded and altered both of them down to the core of their very being.

00:19:05.020 --> 00:19:09.540
But even if they are no longer the Lena and Kane they used to be,

00:19:09.540 --> 00:19:12.280
they are still a Lena and a Kane,

00:19:12.280 --> 00:19:13.960
and their shared experience,

00:19:13.960 --> 00:19:17.480
the way they have absorbed one another into their identities

00:19:17.480 --> 00:19:20.340
has made them into the same.

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:23.640
They are still one person and two alone.

00:19:23.840 --> 00:19:25.660
PUPPET: Yeah, but do the aliens fu--

00:19:25.660 --> 00:19:35.640
[♪♪]

